Part Contents <code>payforge</code> The provider-neutral core: <code>Billing</code>, <code>Connect</code>, <code>CheckStartup</code>, <code>Disabled</code>, <code>ProviderPlanFor</code>, the normalized event, <code>Lifecycle</code>, the ports and in-memory versions of them <code>payforge/stripe</code> The Stripe adapter: <code>Client</code> (customers, checkout, portal, Connect, sync, subscription reads), <code>Webhook</code>, <code>KeyMode</code> <code>payforge/payforgetest</code> Conformance suites for stores, entitlement sinks, sale sinks and seller sinks <code>examples/</code> A catalog sync, a pricing page, a webhook endpoint and limit checks, each run by a test without a Stripe account <code>docs/</code> A user guide: the catalog, checkout and the portal, webhooks, the lifecycle, marketplaces, known limitations <pre><code>if err := payforge.CheckStartup(spec, payforge.ProviderConfig{
